/target
# Local Codex/Claude worktrees and machine-specific settings. Never include
# these when packaging or sharing the repository.
/.claude/
# Benchmark scenes (San Miguel etc., CC-licensed — keep the archive's license
# txt next to the data) live in git LFS (see .gitattributes), with the OBJs
# stored zstd-compressed (.obj.zst — the loader decodes transparently). The
# original download archives and any locally decompressed plain .obj stay
# untracked. Sources: "Real scenes" in CLAUDE.md.
/scenes/*.zip
/scenes/**/*.zip
/scenes/**/*.obj
# Alternate source formats some archives bundle (Intel Sponza ships FBX/MAX/
# USD next to the glTF) — the engine never loads them; they stay in the
# untracked download zips. Ignored so `git add scenes` can't commit gigabytes
# of unusable sources.
/scenes/**/*.fbx
/scenes/**/*.max
/scenes/**/*.usda
/scenes/**/*.usd
/scenes/**/*.usdc
# Intel Sponza is NOT committed. Two independent reasons, either sufficient:
# its terms ("for personal use and educational use", credits_license.txt) do
# not grant redistribution, and at 2.05 GB across 147 files it was 56% of this
# repo's entire LFS payload. It is also the one committed scene the default
# world never loads — world.rs's CURATED table skips it deliberately (2.7 GB of
# 4K PNGs is a texture-memory wall, not a place), so dropping it costs the
# default experience nothing. It remains fully supported as a positional scene
# argument; download it from Intel and drop it here to get the texture-memory
# stress case back:
#   cargo run --release -- scenes/intel-sponza/main_sponza/NewSponza_Main_glTF_003.gltf
# https://www.intel.com/content/www/us/en/developer/topic-technology/graphics-research/samples.html
/scenes/intel-sponza/
# Scene+BVH sidecar caches (src/scene_cache.rs) — per-machine derived
# artifacts, rebuilt on any source/version change. Never commit or LFS them.
*.fcache
*.fcache.*
screenshot_*.png
dlss_gbuf_*.png
oidn_*.png
nppd_*.png
xess_gbuf_*.png
# --check's rendered frame for any NON-default scene (`san-miguel.obj --check`,
# `--check --stress 5000`, the opt-in world). check.png / check_gi.png are the
# TRACKED goldens — the default scene's frame, byte-compared by hand — and a
# scene-keyed run writes here instead so it cannot dirty them. The hyphen is
# what separates the two: the goldens use `_`, these use `-`.
/check-*.png
# The opt-in diagnostic dumps that also land in CWD, for the same reason: a
# `git status` that is only ever dirty when YOU dirtied it is the instrument
# several bit-identity claims in this tree rest on, so nothing a dev lever
# writes belongs in it. FR_CHECK_AB_DUMP's CPU/GPU/diff/water dumps,
# FR_NRD_DEBUG's OUT_VALIDATION frame, FRUSTRACER_HUD_STATS' buffer dump, and
# FR_FSR3_DUMP's input/output pair (the polarity check no magnitude can make —
# see --check-fsr3's U4).
/check_ab_*.png
/nrd-validation.png
/hud-buffer-dump.png
/fsr3-input.png
/fsr3-output.png
# --cinematic output: PNG/PNG16 sequences, EXR masters and encoded video. These
# are working files — often tens of GB for one 4K60 sequence. Only the curated,
# downscaled results under docs/media/ are committed.
/capture/
# Every re-shoot dir (capture-preview, capture-v2, capture-new, ...) — a glob,
# because the enumerated list missed each new dir until someone noticed (a
# 33 MB EXR in one of these reaching plain git history would be permanent).
/capture-*/
/cap-test/
/capture-*.log
# The --frd-lab instrument's per-run tone/log dumps (written to CWD by
# design — the agent Reads them; never committed).
/frd-lab-*.png
*.mp4
*.webm
*.mov
tour-run.log
tour-run.err
gpucheck.log
# ONNX Runtime session-profiling dumps (--check-nppd experiments)
onnxruntime_profile*.json
__pycache__/

# NPPD export workspace: the pinned upstream clone export.py makes for
# itself. The checkpoints and exported .onnx live in the already-ignored
# SDKs/nppd/ (the pretrained weights carry no license grant — never commit
# them or their derivatives; see tools/nppd-export/README.md).
/tools/nppd-export/nppd-upstream/

# Nothing under SDKs/ is committed except the FidelityFX header subset
# whitelisted below. (The Streamline SDK vendoring died with the SL
# retirement — DLSS rides the raw-NGX shims against the non-redistributable
# DLSS SDK at FRUSTRACER_DLSS_SDK, never committed; a stray SL extract here
# stays ignored by the blanket rule.)
/SDKs/*

# FidelityFX SDK: only the MIT-licensed ffx-api / denoiser / upscaler headers
# are committed (vendored from GPUOpen-LibrariesAndSDKs/FidelityFX-SDK @
# v2.3.0; every file carries the MIT block). The signed runtime DLLs come from
# the FidelityFX-Samples-v2.3.0-prebuilt.zip release asset extracted at
# SDKs/FidelityFX-Samples-prebuilt (default --ffx-path points into it) and
# stay ignored with the rest of SDKs/*.
!/SDKs/fidelityfx-sdk/
/SDKs/fidelityfx-sdk/*
!/SDKs/fidelityfx-sdk/api/
!/SDKs/fidelityfx-sdk/denoisers/
!/SDKs/fidelityfx-sdk/upscalers/
!/SDKs/fidelityfx-sdk/framegeneration/
!/SDKs/fidelityfx-sdk/README.md

# NRD: the SOURCE is a git SUBMODULE (SDKs/NRD-src -> NVIDIA-RTX/NRD), which
# vendors nothing — the repo records a URL + a SHA and each clone fetches from
# NVIDIA directly, exactly as install-prerequisites used to fetch the tag zip.
# The blanket /SDKs/* above would otherwise make `git submodule add` refuse.
# The BUILT artifacts stay ignored: they land in SDKs/NRD/bin (outside this
# negation), and the submodule's own _Bin/_Build are covered by its .gitignore.
!/SDKs/NRD-src

# FidelityFX SDK 1.1.4 (the OLDER generation the Vulkan/Metal backends upscale
# with — see install-prerequisites.sh's FFX_SRC_TAG for why two generations
# coexist). The SOURCE stays ignored and is fetched by `install-prerequisites.sh
# fsr3src`; what IS committed is the pre-built SPIR-V shader permutations, and
# they are committed for one reason: the SDK compiles its shaders with
# FidelityFX_SC.exe, a WINDOWS-ONLY tool, and upstream ships no pre-compiled
# SPIR-V. Vendoring the output is what lets a Linux or macOS checkout build FSR3
# at all. MIT and redistributable (unlike every other SDK here), 200 files /
# ~17 MiB of generated C arrays, plain git — and they serve BOTH backends: Metal
# transpiles the same SPIR-V to .metallib at build time. The .h.d depfiles the
# generator drops beside them are build litter and stay out.
!/SDKs/FidelityFX-SDK-prebuilt/
/SDKs/FidelityFX-SDK-prebuilt/shaders/vk/*.h.d
waveviz-*.png

# Crash handler artifacts (src/crash.rs) — the symbolized report and the
# minidump, written next to the exe on a fault. Normally that is target/
# (already ignored); this covers a copied-out exe run from the repo root.
frustracer-crash-*.txt
frustracer-crash-*.dmp

# xwin's package cache — tools/win-cross-check.sh points it at $HOME, but a
# hand-run `xwin splat` defaults to ./.xwin-cache and drops ~886 MB of
# Microsoft packages in the repo root.
/.xwin-cache/
